<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 10 March, from 241 BCE to 2000.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-punic-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">241 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,785 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rome defeats Carthage at the Aegates Islands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A new Roman fleet destroyed a Carthaginian relief fleet off western Sicily. Carthage sued for peace, ending the First Punic War and ceding Sicily, Rome's first overseas province.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1629 <span class="tih-ago">397 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles I dissolves Parliament and begins his Personal Rule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After clashes over taxation and religion, Charles dissolved Parliament and governed without one for eleven years. Financial need forced him to recall it in 1640, leading to civil war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1804 <span class="tih-ago">222 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Upper Louisiana formally passes to the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a ceremony at St Louis, the Spanish flag was lowered and the French tricolour raised, then the next day replaced by the Stars and Stripes. It completed the transfer of the Louisiana Purchase.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1848 <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Senate ratifies the Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate approved the peace with Mexico, which ceded California and much of the Southwest. The United States paid 15 million dollars and assumed its citizens' claims against Mexico.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1876 <span class="tih-ago">150 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bell makes the first telephone call</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his Boston laboratory Alexander Graham Bell spoke into his transmitter: 'Mr Watson, come here, I want to see you.' His assistant Thomas Watson heard him in the next room.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell">Alexander Graham Bell</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1969 <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Earl Ray pleads guilty to killing Martin Luther King Jr.</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ray was sentenced to 99 years in prison. Days later he recanted his plea and sought a trial for the rest of his life, fuelling persistent claims of a conspiracy.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2000 <span class="tih-ago">26 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nasdaq peaks at the height of the dot-com bubble</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The technology-heavy Nasdaq Composite index closed at 5,048, more than double its level a year earlier. It then fell by nearly 80 per cent by October 2002 as internet stocks collapsed.</p></div></li></ol>
